// The spall cone's shape and its calibration — the field thrown from every body exit a round
// reaches —, and a burst's field. Read by `src/ballistics/spall_cone.rs`, embedded and parsed once,
// validated at parse.
// The law itself (strength, the ball law's centre-weighted profile, shadowing, dose) is design doc
// §5, `.agents/docs/design/armor-penetration-and-damage.md`; this file holds its shape data and its
// calibration: the number that converts its dose to HP points and the calibre that number was set
// against, the reference a cone's hole-area term is measured from. A cone's half-angle and profile
// are not here: both follow from its field's ratio, the exit layer's substance's
// (`debris_half_angle_deg` in `assets/materials/materials.ron`).
//
// Every value here is a choice the owner can change by editing this file alone; none is a
// constant of the law. The playtest fork on the axis is F5 in
// `.agents/scratch/playtest-forks/README.md`.
//
// PROVENANCE: every value is authored `(value, Kind("source or reason"))`, Kind one of Measured,
// Derived, Tuned, Resolution, Unknown (`src/provenance.rs`); a value without one does not load.
(
    // The cone's axis. `RearNormalBisector`: normalize(rear-face outward normal + exit direction)
    // at a genuine exit, the exit direction at an internal step (which has no face).
    // `ExitDirection`: the exit direction everywhere.
    axis: (RearNormalBisector, Tuned("engineering assumption (playtest fork F5) with MEASURED
        support: debris axis about halfway between the shot line and the plate normal, 25°
        measured against 22.5° predicted at 45° obliquity (Verolme 1997, Recht & Howell 1967;
        research/cloud-angle-deep.md)")),

    // N, the number of directions the cone is sampled by, in equal-solid-angle strata of 1/N of the
    // cone each, every one weighted by its stratum's share of the field. The emitted total is S/2
    // at every N, so N changes how finely a box's dose is resolved, never how much the cone
    // carries.
    directions: (64, Tuned("owner decision 2026-10-17 ('64 for now'), the cost against the
        resolution: one throw under the ball law MEASURED 2026-10-24 by
        ballistics::pen_cam::spall_law_cost (release, macOS arm64, best of 9, the 7 cones of the
        penetrating scenarios): 0.30 ms at N = 24, 0.64 at 64, 1.23 at 128, 2.29 at 256; the dose
        step per direction on the s1 cone at 64 runs from 9.3 HP on the axis to 0.58 HP at the
        rim, 5.6 HP on average (DERIVED: S·f_k × 70 HP per reference-mm / 64, S = 10.18
        reference-mm). The count changes how finely a box's dose is resolved, never the emitted
        total")),

    // The field's calibration: HP points per reference-mm of field dose, where the line converts
    // at `ballistics::HP_PER_REFERENCE_MM`. A field deposit of d reference-mm enters a box's
    // per-shot dose as d × this / that, in whole dose units; the cone's strength S stays in
    // reference-mm. It sets the potency of every cone at once and nothing else: the shape and the
    // field law both conserve a cone's emitted total.
    hp_per_reference_mm: (70, Tuned("owner decision 2026-10-23 (#2 in
        .agents/scratch/damage-cam-2026-10-08/research/ap-aphe-2026-10-23/decision-2026-10-23.md):
        the 30 HP crew pool (box_classes.ron) at a 0.2 m² mean face, a seated crew member's and
        so a crew box's in a tank's sim geometry, is emptied within about 2 m of the hole on the
        recorded s1 cone, a weak ordinary perforation; kept at 70 under the ball law (owner
        decision 2026-10-23, night, same
        file), which keeps every cone's emitted total and moves its potency toward the axis.
        DERIVED: a box of face A at distance R fully inside a cone of half-angle α, at angle θ off
        its axis, catches 2 f(θ) A / (R² Ω_c) of its emission E = S/2, Ω_c = 2π(1 − cos α) and
        f(θ) the ball's weight there (½ averaged over the cone), so its knockout radius is
        R = sqrt(2 f(θ) E A / (pool Ω_c)). On the s1 cone (S/2 = 5.09 reference-mm through RHA,
        α = 26.2°, Ω_c = 0.646 sr) that is 1.92 m at an average spot and 2.49 m on the axis
        (f = 0.842), against 0.73 m and 0.94 m at the line's 10 HP per reference-mm. The seed
        tank's crew box, 0.4 × 0.3 × 0.7 m at a MEASURED 0.2033 m² mean face, gives 1.93 m and
        2.51 m (DERIVED)")),

    // d_ref (m), the calibre `hp_per_reference_mm` was set against. A cone's strength goes as the
    // area of the hole its round's penetrator made, (d / d_ref)² of a hole of calibre d (design
    // doc §5; the exponent is the law, not data), so a round of this calibre throws its cone
    // unscaled and every other is measured from it. Finite, positive and normal.
    reference_calibre_m: (0.088, Tuned("the calibre the field's rate was set against")),

    // A burst's field (design doc §5a, "The burst"): thrown from the burst point about the round's
    // flight direction, its ratio the carried speed over the burst's greatest sideways speed v_s,
    // through the struck tank's volumes, passing as the spall cone's directions do, its dose
    // converting at `hp_per_reference_mm`. The ring and the ball are the two burst shapes a round's
    // burst block names (`assets/rounds/`).
    burst: (
        // The burst's strength S (reference-mm) per kJ of its driven mass's kinetic energy
        // ½ M v_s² (the wall under the ring, the round less its core under the ball); the field
        // emits S/2 in all.
        reference_mm_per_kj: (1.0, Tuned("provisional: a crew box presenting a 0.2 m² face (a
            seated crew member's) fully inside the ball at rest, 2.0 m from the burst, has its 30
            HP pool (box_classes.ron) emptied. DERIVED: at rest the ball is uniform over the
            sphere, so the box catches A/(4πR²) of the emission E = S/2, and its knockout radius is
            R = sqrt(E A × 70 / (30 × 4π)); R = 2.0 m needs E = 107.7 reference-mm, S = 215.4,
            against the shipped ball round's 214.8 kJ: 1.003 per kJ, rounded to 1.0, R = 2.00 m")),
        // h (degrees): the ring spans θ_c − h to θ_c + h of polar angle from the flight axis,
        // θ_c = atan(1/λ), uniform over that band; its near edge is held at the axis.
        ring_half_width_deg: (10.0, Tuned("provisional (owner's brief 4b): the band the wall's
            fragments leave in, one datum for every ring")),
        // N for each burst law, as `directions` is for the cone: the emitted total is S/2 at every
        // N, so N sets how finely a box's dose is resolved, never how much the burst carries. One
        // throw's cost MEASURED 2026-10-24 by ballistics::pen_cam::burst_law_cost (release, macOS
        // arm64, best of 9, s1's line fired with each burst round). At rest each direction
        // carries S/2 × 70 / N HP points of dose (DERIVED, the field uniform over its support).
        ring_directions: (256, Tuned("provisional, flagged for the owner: the cost against the
            resolution. The ring's throw: 0.50 ms at N = 64, 1.47 at 256, 4.01 at 684; at rest
            115, 29 and 11 HP points per direction (S = 211.1), so at 256 one direction is about
            one crew pool")),
        ball_directions: (256, Tuned("provisional, flagged for the owner: the cost against the
            resolution. The ball's throw: 0.41 ms at N = 64, 0.99 at 256, 3.26 at 684; at rest
            117, 29 and 11 HP points per direction (S = 214.8), so at 256 one direction is about
            one crew pool")),
    ),
)
